okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Backup still slow; 'stored' looked stuck while 'read' grew (menu backup of G:/ciel-Walkie to local target G:/backup/andy)."
reported: "User, 2026-10-11, screenshot: 'Backing up: 28694 files, 7413.5 MB read, 349.8 MB stored (270 s)', '저장되는게 안늘어나고 고정인거같은데', '아직도 파일 카피 속도가 많이 늦는거아 더 향상시킬수는없ㅈ나'. Plan approved 2026-10-11 ('승인')."
observed:
  live_run: "PID 33516 (6638f33) 'backup create --cwd G:/ciel-Walkie', started 20:48:34. Progress file at 21:08: 70,049 files, 120.6 GB read, 26.7 GB stored; current files under .local/release-check-0.4.2xx (many release copies). Process IO over 10 s: read 215 MB/s, write 74 MB/s, 0.6 CPU cores, total CPU 60%, disk idle 83%."
  live_run_end: "Its manifest 20261012T022611Z-c4b13b was written 21:26 (111,230 files, 157.5 GB read, 41.3 GB stored, ~38 min), but the menu recorded the run as 'cancelled' at 22:23 with no id: see stall_after_saving."
  stored_flat: "G:/backup/andy had no snapshots folder but held 46,761 blobs (14.17 GB) written before this run (oldest 2026-10-10 12:30): earlier runs never finished. Chunks already in the store are not counted as stored, so 'stored' stays flat while those files are re-read."
  no_files_cache: "session_backup_collect/ops re-read and re-hashed every file on every backup; no reuse of the previous manifest (grep: no such code)."
  small_file_profile: "bench.py, 10,000 new 20 KB files, C: scratch, jobs 8: first backup 104.9 s, of which io.open 92.4 s on the main thread (9.2 ms/open); same files again 7.7 s (io.open 0.4 s)."
  parallel_open: "opens.py, 4,000 newly written files each: 1 reader 9.72 ms/file, 8 readers 1.05 ms/file, 16 readers 0.57 ms/file."
  defender: "Get-MpComputerStatus: RealTimeProtectionEnabled True, OnAccessProtectionEnabled True. That on-access scanning causes the first-open cost is likely but not proven (no exclusion test; changing security settings is not allowed)."
  preflight_walk: "real-run-1.log: every backup to a local target walked the whole work folder first ('measuring', 99,585 files, ~150 s on G:) although a target that already holds a snapshot only needs min(total, 1 GB) free (session_backup_cli.preflight)."
  stall_after_saving: "pipe_block.py/.txt: a child that writes more than 4096 bytes to a PIPE does not exit until the parent reads (4096 exits, 4200 blocks). run_backup only read after the child exited. The c4b13b summary rebuilt from its manifest (result_size.py) is ~4.8 KB, so that run very likely sat blocked on stdout from 21:26 until it was cancelled at 22:23 (the exact bytes of that run's output are not recoverable). run_backup_big_summary.txt: same ~70 KB summary, old code 'stopped after 15 s', new code ok in 0.1 s."
  summary_decoding: "First real run of the new code (real-run-1.log, task output): the parent decoded the child's UTF-8 JSON with the Windows code page and failed (UnicodeDecodeError: 'charmap' codec can't decode byte 0x9d); ciel_runtime.py:556 reconfigures the child's stdout to UTF-8. The old code used the same text=True decoding, hidden behind the stall. The snapshot (20261012T050254Z-a09f91) was saved; the state file was left at running=True until the next run."
changes:
  - "session_backup_collect: files of a tree are read, hashed and handed to the writer on writer.jobs reader threads; entries still come out in walk order (READ_AHEAD 256 queued, a queued file holds no data). Secrets, split JSON and SQLite stay on the main thread."
  - "session_backup_collect: each file/jsonl entry records sig = size:mtime_ns:file id (+ ctime_ns off Windows) taken before reading, and the manifest records 'started'. previous_files() takes the newest snapshot of the workspace on every target and keeps the entries all of them recorded alike (same sig and chunks) under the same root path, modified at least 2 s before that snapshot started; such files are not read again and their chunks are named again. A target without a snapshot, or an older manifest without sig/started, means every file is read."
  - "session_backup_store.ChunkWriter: write() takes a lock (called from reader threads); reuse() counts reused files; stats gain reused_files / reused_bytes."
  - "session_backup_ops.create_snapshot(full=False): loads the newest manifest per target (newest_manifest) unless full; CLI 'backup create --full'; menu row 'Full backup now' (value now-full); progress line '<n> files (<m> unchanged)'; result line '...; <m> unchanged files not read again'."
  - "session_backup_cli.preflight: skips the folder walk when every local target already holds a snapshot of the workspace and has at least 1 GB free (the answer cannot change); still walks for a first backup or a nearly full target."
  - "session_backup_service.run_backup: communicate(timeout=poll) instead of poll()+sleep, so the child's output is read while it runs; Popen and the menu/MCP 'list' calls decode child output as UTF-8 (errors=replace)."
  - "session_backup_collect._start: one stat per file instead of is_file()+stat() (no measurable change: 3.3 s -> 3.2 s on 10,002 unchanged files)."
verification:
  unit_tests: "scripts/run_test_group.py unit, CIEL_RUNTIME_* unset: 1850 tests OK (skipped 49). New: unchanged files not read and same chunks, --full reads all, changed/replaced (same size+mtime, new file id)/grown jsonl re-read, mtime within 2 s of the last snapshot re-read, a target without the snapshot means a full read, CLI/menu row/progress text, parallel reads overlap (>1 at once) with the same entry order as jobs 1, preflight walks only when needed, a 70 KB UTF-8 summary with Korean text does not stall run_backup."
  bench: "bench_compare.py (C: scratch, 10,002 new files: 10,000 x ~20 KB + 2 x 200 MB, jobs 8). Old (6638f33): first 97.9 s, unchanged 5.6 s, 100 changed 6.6 s. New: first 11.6 s, unchanged 3.3 s (10,002 reused), 100 changed 3.3 s (9,902 reused, 100 chunks uploaded)."
  real_first_run: "real-run-1.log, G:/ciel-Walkie -> andy through run_backup, new code, existing manifest without sig: measuring ~150 s, reading 110,121 files / 156.7 GB in ~680 s, total ~864 s (previous run ~38 min). Snapshot 20261012T050254Z-a09f91 saved; summary decoding failed (fixed afterwards, see summary_decoding)."
  real_menu_run: "menu-run-2/ (menu_e2e.py + menu_drive.py: real menu window, 18. Session backup -> Back up this session now, this checkout): no measuring step, finished in 101 s; 'Saved snapshot 20261012T052110Z-d91d9a to andy. incremental: 628 of 124807 chunks new, 20.4 MB uploaded (snapshot 150290.4 MB); 111225 unchanged files not read again.'; menu summary 'last 10-12 00:21 ok'. Screens are cropped/redacted (the full menu shows provider URL and key hints; raw kept outside the repo)."
  chunks_present: "check_chunks.txt: d91d9a names 69,020 distinct chunks, 0 missing in G:/backup/andy/blobs; 111,463 of 113,224 entries have the same chunks as a09f91 (the full read)."
not_verified:
  - "A full 'Verify a snapshot' (reads every chunk, ~150 GB) was not run on d91d9a; existence of every chunk was checked instead."
  - "NAS (Synology) target with reuse: covered only by the same code path; newest_manifest reads one manifest per target over the network."
  - "Files whose mtime a tool sets back while keeping size and file id would be reused; 'Full backup now' reads everything."
side_findings:
  - "During the run two 32de611 Codex launchers (cli --continue, since 04:40/04:44) each did ~9,300 reads/s, ~75 MB/s and ~21,000 other I/O ops/s (top_io.ps1). Which files and which disk is not known; not investigated (live sessions)."
other_test_groups: "runtime 405 OK, router 1188 OK, 9611 health 200. channel: 1 of 3 runs OK, the others failed different BoundaryScanDeadlineTests / test_resumed_codex_session...; the same group on unmodified HEAD (git archive 6638f33) failed 1 of 4 runs on the same tests, and this change touches no channel file: pre-existing timing flakiness, not caused here."
stale_running_state:
  observed: "After the crashed parent of real-run-1 the state file kept running=True; the menu showed 'last running since 10-11 22:23' (menu-run-2/menu-backup-progress.png) and mcp_session_backup create refuses while running is set (session_backup_service.py: 'a backup of this workspace is already running')."
  change: "workspace_state(): running counts only while the workspace's backup lock is held by a live process; otherwise it reports running=False, interrupted=True, and the menu shows '<start> interrupted'. (User 2026-10-12: '아직 수정할사항잇으면 수정'.)"
  verification: "test_a_backup_whose_process_died_is_not_running_any_more: dead lock holder -> not running, menu 'interrupted', MCP create starts; live holder -> 'running since'. unit 1851 OK."
